--login retains automatic owner entry for compatibility. Ordinary /signin email sign-in sends only through a configured remote mail provider with real credentials; no sender is configured by default. --stop stops the owned server.","preview":"Serve the built Oncall app on a loopback address with local state and owner sign-in. Ordinary /signin email sign-in sends only through a configured remote mail provider with real credentials; no sender is configured by default. --stop stops the owned server.","build":"See SEED-COMMAND-CONTRACT.md for build effects.","verify":"See SEED-COMMAND-CONTRACT.md for verify effects.","reset":"See SEED-COMMAND-CONTRACT.md for reset effects.","deploy":"Deploy incident coordination to your own Cloudflare account, claim the configured owner and retire its one-time setup token. Requires Cloudflare credentials and configured remote sign-in mail. Paging stays OFF; keep your existing pager active. --remove --yes deletes owned resources and reads back their absence. --site publishes the separate Run site. --dry-run builds and validates a local plan without credentials or Cloudflare requests and changes nothing remotely. It does not check target secrets, deployment permissions, remote readiness or mail delivery. --site --dry-run builds the separate Run site with no provider request.","export":"Write a private local archive of supported durable records and import journal; exclude sessions, credentials and private settings. Stop dev and preview first.","import":"Require an empty local destination and explicit --yes; atomically restore validated records and journal, pause pending timers, hold handoff approvals and disable Business import intake. Credentials and sessions never transfer; new owners must explicitly map an archived administrator identity.","doctor":"See SEED-COMMAND-CONTRACT.md for doctor effects.","describe":"See SEED-COMMAND-CONTRACT.md for describe effects.","check":"See SEED-COMMAND-CONTRACT.md for check effects.","release":"See SEE