-use grant for the recorded owner into that deployment's auth database, then prints the link once to this terminal; it is never saved. The link works once, only for that owner, expires within 15 minutes, and its use is recorded in the owner's audit log. Signed in this way, the owner can correct a wrong email in settings."}}},"unavailable":{"check":{"ok":true,"exitCode":0},"describe":{"cliVersion":"0.2.108","profile":"first-party","effects":{"install":"See SEED-COMMAND-CONTRACT.md for install effects.","setup":"Build and migrate local state, save the first owner and private settings, and retain existing owner, secrets and data on repeat setup. No provider request.","dev":"Run Oncall on a loopback address, applying local migrations and printing a private RER_OPEN owner entry. First launch confirms the read-only owner at /setup; later launches open the app. --as signed-out selects the signed-out persona; --login retains automatic owner entry for compatibility. Ordinary /signin email sign-in sends only through a configured remote mail provider with real credentials; no sender is configured by default. --stop stops the owned server.","preview":"Serve the built Oncall app on a loopback address with local state and owner sign-in. Ordinary /signin email sign-in sends only through a configured remote mail provider with real credentials; no sender is configured by default. --stop stops the owned server.","build":"See SEED-COMMAND-CONTRACT.md for build effects.","verify":"See SEED-COMMAND-CONTRACT.md for verify effects.","reset":"See SEED-COMMAND-CONTRACT.md for reset effects.","deploy":"Deploy incident coordination to your own Cloudflare account, claim the configured owner and retire its one-time setup token. Requires Cloudflare credentials and configured remote sign-in mail. Paging stays OFF; keep your existing pager active. --remove --yes deletes owned resources and reads back their absence. --site publishes the separate Run site. --dry-run builds and validates a local plan